-- title:
--   Finite-suffix observation-abort mass is at most $3M2^{-T}$
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$ with $n>0$, and let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids of common rank $r$ on the full $n$-element ground set. Let $o_1,o_2$ be exact independence oracles, and assume the two matroids have at least one common base. Let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)$ have rational entries in $(0,1)$ and let $s$ be the setup schedule, with $L$ phases, $M$ observations, draw cap $T$, cooling factor $\rho$, and ratio tolerance $\eta$. Fix $j<L$.
--
--   Call a phase certified when its actual transition succeeds, multiplies the stored product by a ratio whose relative error against the exact consecutive transversal-partition ratio lies between $(1-\eta)/(1+\eta)$ and $(1+\eta)/(1-\eta)$, and its current multipliers and stored tables at levels no later than the current phase lie within factors $1/4$ and $4$ of the appropriate transversal-to-defect partition ratios, both before the transition and after it when another phase remains. Let $m$ be the prescribed run block length for $(n,r,p)$. Assume a finite bit string $a$ is a successful phase prefix: some length-$m$ tape has all phases below $j$ certified, and $a$ is that tape truncated at the tape cursor reached before phase $j$.
--
--   Put $t=\max(m-|a|,0)$. For each suffix $b\in\{0,1\}^t$, run the algorithm on $ab$, reading zero beyond its end. Let $E$ be the set of those suffixes for which all earlier phases are certified, phase history at $j$ is present, its restart succeeds, and the ensuing observation phase with parameter $\rho^j$ aborts. Then $$|E|\,2^{-t}\le3M\,2^{-T}.$$ This controls the uniform suffix mass of the joint restart-success and observation-failure event.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalObservationAbortMass.lean#L171-L304

